Alignment, thermal state and geometric verification (@mech-alignment: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mechanical-engineering, #source "../sources/Bearing-Maintenance-Handbook-SKF.lingua#r_2KXP88XVRZAFSYK92QAM6QYYRV", #source "../sources/Precision-Machine-Design-Hale-Thesis.lingua#r_3V7NVTW0ER7HDK3BJ1HCNPZYN4", #mechanical-engineering "Commissioning-acceptance-and-validation-of-use.lingua#r_4K9PKAGC72FHH0SBDCEDTWGHF8") { r_4S1JS0TG093GXKSQ2AJSCQB4HH
**Read:** [Bearing maintenance handbook — SKF, 2011](../sources/Bearing-Maintenance-Handbook-SKF.lingua#r_2KXP88XVRZAFSYK92QAM6QYYRV), chapter 6; [Principles and Techniques for Designing Precision Machines — Hale](../sources/Precision-Machine-Design-Hale-Thesis.lingua#r_3V7NVTW0ER7HDK3BJ1HCNPZYN4), alignment and error separation; the shared dimensional-metrology guidance.

Alignment concerns the relative positions and directions that matter to function. A dial indicator or laser gives readings through its own geometry, reference and mounting. Separate instrument setup error, shaft/housing geometry and the actual relative axis. Soft-foot or foundation movement can change alignment when bolts are tightened.

Cold alignment may differ from operating alignment because of load and temperature. Measure or model the paths that move the relevant interfaces. A flexible coupling can tolerate some motion while still transmitting unwanted restoring forces.

**Work:** Derive the readings expected from a known offset and angular misalignment. Use reversal or an independent setup to separate an artifact from the machine. Repeat under a declared load/thermal state and after a controlled disassembly. State what alignment claim the data support and what motion remains unmeasured.

**Return:** [Mechanical engineering and machine design](../Mechanical-engineering-and-machine-design.lingua#r_0017YZ63HZBZ4P4WD8DECVWE4R).
